1 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534857 true] [17592186315343 1100 "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x?$" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315343 1113 #uuid "2022b58f-f48d-5794-93ee-d709576b1e72" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315343 1145 "First, notice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[-3,3].$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\in [-3,3].$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =c \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\frac{c}{3}+2\\pi n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ can be any integer. \n\nNotice that the equations $x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\frac{c}{3}+2\\pi n$ do not depend on $y.$ So, for a given $c\\in [-3,3]$ and integer $n$, the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of vertical lines, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/cdd8cec2d30ff2956d5210a49036c17d99781d0b62c0b0f42f97d0575c4d80f6.png)" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315344 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315345 13194139534857 true] [17592186315344 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315346 13194139534857 true] [17592186315344 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315347 13194139534857 true] [17592186315344 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315348 13194139534857 true] [17592186315344 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315349 13194139534857 true] [17592186315344 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534857 true] [17592186315344 1041 "selection" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315344 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315346 13194139534857 true] [17592186315344 1110 #uuid "6da9e415-1b08-5085-a961-0a9b17583025" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315345 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/d774c444ad33c68ec5d507611324030f2005671265ba5f855f322d8db57b69b4.png" 13194139534857 true] [