0 1113 #uuid "384942ae-d22a-5af8-bd31-df40d8002920" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315350 1145 "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-x) & =c \\\\ y-x & ={e}^{c} \\\\ y & =x+{e}^{c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of lines with slope of $1.$ Also, note that ${e}^{c}>0$ for all $c.$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/c115999648577bfb60015f0e54dd0c6d6de22076e87026ba94c49e56207144e0.png)" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315352 13194139534857 true] [17592186315351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315353 13194139534857 true] [17592186315351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315354 13194139534857 true] [17592186315351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315355 13194139534857 true] [17592186315351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315356 13194139534857 true] [17592186315351 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534857 true] [17592186315351 1041 "selection" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315351 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315353 13194139534857 true] [17592186315351 1110 #uuid "f114d5bd-02f5-561a-b38f-b1e77e82f08f" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315352 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/93cd9ed4c9c1507d1ff828abbb697cd72ab8ebdb7d44a1033d6e99a1eed9e633.png" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315352 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534857 true] [17592186315352 1111 #uuid "b33d2d55-9247-5827-bc48-5fe8359aff9e" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315353 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/c115999648577bfb60015f0e54dd0c6d6de22076e87026ba94c49e56207144e0.png" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315353 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534857 true] [17592186315353 1111 #uuid "f7398a10-dbe5-5d53-a120-9b78334c0583" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315354 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/0bedc560b7b18c2a6841313d888dde7349b66f2514ce8c222af7ef2fc0bc9546.png" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315354 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534857 true] [17592186315354 1111 #uuid "a9bcb7bb-e270-55c8-9058-369970de6dc9" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315355 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/5155660bc0e9957b1a33cc6fbd933ba10618be07911f9384255bc703f7925ba7.png" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315355 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534857 true] [17592186315355 1111 #uuid "9a29ba99-6f02-511a-a252-ca34e48a8196" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315356 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/d5e28121cd5847f3119a9fb33a57dd2d86e2f12bff3061ef64182b12c1ace178.png" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315356 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534857 true] [17592186315356 1111 #uuid "2d320065-896c-59e5-a66b-0332de590f38" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315357 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315358 13194139534857 true] [17592186315357 1089 "q-36825" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315357 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534857 true] [17592186315357 1100 "Find the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $Q(1,1)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315357 1113 #uuid "88de5b2b-c4a7-5648-97ab-7bd71becc10f" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315357 1145 "First, we find the value of the function at $Q$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1) & =\\frac{2(1)}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $Q(1,1)$ is the $1$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=1.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ 2y & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2y+1 & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $Q(1,1)$ is the circle ${x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1.$" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315359 13194139534857 true] [17592186315358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315360 13194139534857 true] [17592186315358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315361 13194139534857 true] [17592186315358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315362 13194139534857 true] [17592186315358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315363 13194139534857 true] [17592186315358 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534857 true] [17592186315358 1041 "selection" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315358 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315363 13194139534857 true] [17592186315358 1110 #uuid "0a5648bc-2d5d-50b2-bc64-b499dee8031b" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315359 1034 "y-1={x}^{2}" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315359 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534857 true] [17592186315359 1111 #uuid "2644416a-2708-5a03-930c-66a23991e6a4" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315360 1034 "(y-1)^{2}-{x}^{2}=1" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315360 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534857 true] [17592186315360 1111 #uuid "52df9c01-7d93-5dc5-b6f3-e1973808d10e" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315361 1034 "x=\\pm (y-1)" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315361 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534857 true] [17592186315361 1111 #uuid "17b82f06-5c30-5722-9ec9-52062d470c19" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315362 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315362 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534857 true] [17592186315362 1111 #uuid "0eba554c-49d3-502f-8487-efcda0fdf618" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315363 1034 "{x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315363 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534857 true] [17592186315363 1111 #uuid "bce5cec0-bae9-584d-b30e-58a502515f54" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315364 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315365 13194139534857 true] [17592186315364 1089 "q-64909" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315364 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534857 true] [17592186315364 1100 "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)={e}^{xy}?$" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315364 1113 #uuid "2e086daf-480c-5185-b9b5-74c8b16950ea" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315364 1145 "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only level curves for $c>0.$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ {e}^{xy} & =c \\\\ xy & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡c \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡c}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can split this into three cases, depending on the sign of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c.$\n\n- Case 1: $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c>0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡c}{x}.$\n\n- Case 2: $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c=0.$ In this case, we have the lines $x=0$ and $y=0.$\n\n- Case 3: $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c<0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $y=-\\frac{|\\operatorname{ln}⁡c|}{x}.$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of hyperbolas centered at the origin. Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/d330ddb12d1df9d31af3d082b04271d02df381739064a6fe2203dabce358a09f.png)" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315366 13194139534857 true] [17592186315365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315367 13194139534857 true] [17592186315365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315368 13194139534857 true] [17592186315365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315369 13194139534857 true] [17592186315365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315370 13194139534857 true] [17592186315365 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534857 true] [17592186315365 1041 "selection" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315365 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315367 13194139534857 true] [17592186315365 1110 #uuid "ff473d8e-0f42-5030-81e1-4037a4f4b557" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315366 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/57f87a716b14698d0087bc65e9abdc04776bd4b7addaaf172a4e5f0a5f38ea6a.png" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534857 true] [17592186315366 1111 #uuid "5e55dc49-24f9-5af9-97cd-895a5ccc1ed3" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315367 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/d330ddb12d1df9d31af3d082b04271d02df381739064a6fe2203dabce358a09f.png" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315367 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534857 true] [17592186315367 1111 #uuid "2735966f-9783-5290-9cf9-d4434b337ca1" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315368 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/24b6123a1f641df32cdc19ec77d999dac5584b9693ae92ce9c1e618f67487473.png" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315368 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534857 true] [17592186315368 1111 #uuid "40b3212b-c714-502c-a01d-763a17dceaaa" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315369 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/836e10a411261b1ef2cb8146aed75c40326f278487e5843c57f10f65b9cc3f05.png" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315369 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534857 true] [17592186315369 1111 #uuid "5220b7e6-a9f1-5521-94d6-7b605f285077" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315370 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/ef3171d89bff6a2a6ef105f81a9fe60959f2d760634039cd8fb0f70cf8c2cc9e.png" 131