$V(2,2)$ is the circle ${x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4.$" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315379 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315380 13194139534857 true] [17592186315379 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315381 13194139534857 true] [17592186315379 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315382 13194139534857 true] [17592186315379 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315383 13194139534857 true] [17592186315379 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315384 13194139534857 true] [17592186315379 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534857 true] [17592186315379 1041 "selection" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315379 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315382 13194139534857 true] [17592186315379 1110 #uuid "b1e67d35-43a8-5928-9aba-42ff24fbff92" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315380 1034 "(y-2)^{2}-{x}^{2}=4" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315380 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534857 true] [17592186315380 1111 #uuid "26d6f0e3-d9bb-5b88-a772-65a698498c30" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315381 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315381 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534857 true] [17592186315381 1111 #uuid "f86d1dc6-7204-5eb1-971c-ccbacf31d7e1" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315382 1034 "{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315382 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534857 true] [17592186315382 1111 #uuid "11867973-a8e0-5370-9271-65bef0969ffa" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315383 1034 "4x=\\pm (y-2)" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315383 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534857 true] [17592186315383 1111 #uuid "1487a2b1-2a61-5b99-bef3-7ab05e64a212" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315384 1034 "y-2=4{x}^{2}" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315384 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534857 true] [17592186315384 1111 #uuid "65472bbf-82dd-511b-bc15-fc74b6108845" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315385 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315386 13194139534857 true] [17592186315385 1089 "q-71391" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315385 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534857 true] [17592186315385 1100 "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4}{{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=3$ gives a hyperbola\n- $c=0$ gives an ellipse\n- $c=1$ gives a circle" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315385 1113 #uuid "f59b0ead-9e6c-5643-b77d-cab71602ea67" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315385 1145 "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4}{{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4 & =c{y}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+(3-c){y}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=3$ then the level curves are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{2},$ which consists of two vertical lines.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}=4,$ which is an ellipse.\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2,$ which is a circle.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true." 13194139534857 true] [17592186315386 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315387 13194139534857 true] [17592186315386 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315388 13194139534857 true] [17592186315386 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315389 13194139534857 true] [17592186315386 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315390 13194139534857 true] [17592186315386 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315391 13194139534857 true] [17592186315386 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534857 true] [17592186315386 1041 "selection" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315386 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315387 13194139534857 true] [17592186315386 1110 #uuid "ea178ba4-3b2d-56d1-a758-c52013fee9fa" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315387 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315387 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534857 true] [17592186315387 1111 #uuid "aac0359d-5ee4-5610-b651-6924e0ef731f" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315388 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315388 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534857 true] [17592186315388 1111 #uuid "eee63a1d-98d4-5e84-ab26-ff7cd9428d66" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315389 1034 "I only" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315389 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534857 true] [17592186315389 1111 #uuid "acd04519-a14e-5a48-aa69-c4da3afa7257" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315390 1034 "III only" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315390 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534857 true] [17592186315390 1111 #uuid "76214168-f2f5-511f-95d8-2b38da4025ea" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315391 1034 "II only" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315391 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534857 true] [17592186315391 1111 #uuid "a750f04d-4cf1-50ef-90c2-95f6c8366994" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315392 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315393 13194139534857 true] [17592186315392 1089 "q-71401" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315392 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534857 true] [17592186315392 1100 "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2{y}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=1$ gives an ellipse\n- $c=2$ gives two lines\n- $c=3$ gives a hyperbola" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315392 1113 #uuid "89b4a109-08c5-568a-830b-41c72ba008a5" 13194139534857 true] [17592186315392 1145 "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{y}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ 2{y}^{2}+1 & =c({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\ c{x}^{2}+(c-2){y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=1,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curves are $x=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},$ which consists of two vertical lines.\n\n- If $c=3$ then the level curve is $3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ which is an ellipse.\n\nSo, only statement II is true." 13194139534857 true] [17592186315393 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315394 13194139534857 true] [17592186315393 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315395 13194139534857 true] [17592186315393 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315396 13194139534857 true] [17592186315393 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315397 13194139534857 true] [17592186315393 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315398 13194139534857 true] [17592186315393 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534857 true] [17592186315393 1041 "selection" 13194139534857 true] [17